## Architecture Boundaries

- Respect the current project directory structure under `ecommerce-platform/`:
  - `backend/` (NestJS API + Prisma)
  - `frontend/` (Next.js storefront)
  - `admin/` (Next.js admin panel)
- Keep app boundaries strict: no cross-app runtime imports between `backend`, `frontend`, and `admin`.
- Do not create redundant, nested, or duplicate configuration files.
- Treat `ecommerce-platform/docs/Architecture.md` as the canonical architecture reference.

## Frontend Theme And Styling Boundaries

- Use `ecommerce-platform/frontend/tailwind.config.ts` as the single source of truth for brand tokens:
  - `brand.primary: #4F90F1`
  - `brand.secondary: #EEF4FE`
  - `brand.accent: #3577D9`
  - `brand.text: #1A2E40`
  - `brand.bg: #E2EEFC`
- Keep `boxShadow.product-card` defined exactly once in `tailwind.config.ts`.
- Do not duplicate brand token declarations in `ecommerce-platform/frontend/app/globals.css` `@theme`.
- In `globals.css`, only map semantic tokens (`--color-primary`, `--color-background`, etc.) from theme variables.
- For UI/layout color updates, do not hardcode inline hex colors in TSX/CSS when a `brand-*` token can be used.
- Header/Footer chrome must use unified blue styling from brand tokens; nav links and icons on chrome must remain readable (`text-white` when on blue backgrounds).

## Stability And Reflection Rules

- Before modifying any file, read the full file first.
- Do not introduce duplicate object keys, duplicate routes, duplicate config keys, or conflicting CSS class/property definitions.
- Preserve current core functionality unless explicitly asked to overhaul:
  - Prisma models and migrations
  - Zustand state stores
  - Search/filter logic
  - Checkout and cart flows
- For frontend API integration changes, extend existing API client patterns rather than creating parallel networking layers.

## Backend Boundaries

- Keep data-model and persistence logic in `ecommerce-platform/backend/` only.
- Respect route domain boundaries and guards:
  - Public storefront routes
  - `/admin/*` routes with admin auth/permissions
- Keep cart/checkout ephemeral storage behavior aligned with current Redis/in-memory strategy unless explicitly changed.

## Cleanup And Quality Assurance

- After each set of file changes, run formatting/lint checks in affected app(s) to catch syntax regressions:
  - `frontend`: `npm run lint`
  - `backend`: `npm run lint`
  - `admin`: `npm run lint`
- Resolve introduced syntax issues (dangling brackets, malformed objects/classes, duplicate keys) before finishing.
- Preserve icon visibility and contrast in structural components (header/footer).

## Working Principles

- Minimize diff scope and avoid unrelated refactors.
- Reuse existing conventions and utilities before adding new abstractions.
- Do not commit or push unless explicitly requested.
